<title>SOUTH KOREA: Two S.Korean firms buy 21,500T of U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>Two S.Korean firms buy 21,500T of U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Cheiljedang Corp and Dongah Flour Mills Co Ltd said on Thursday they jointly bought 21,500 tonnes of U.S. wheat from Japanese trading house Toshoku Ltd.  </p>
<p>Shipment was set for January 15-February 15 from the Pacific Northwest to the southeastern port city of Pusan.</p>
<p>Details for the results obtained by trading sources are as follows:</p>
<p>Dongah Flour Mills Co Ltd</p>
<p> Type of Wheat	   Tonne   Price/Tonne(FOB)</p>
<p> Soft White		5,300   $143.55</p>
<p>(protein max 10.8%)  </p>
<p>  Soft White		2,000   $142.45</p>
<p>(protein max 9.5%)</p>
<p>  Hard Red Winter	 3,700   $174.35</p>
<p>  Dark Northern Spring    500   $175.35</p>
<p>Cheiljedang Corp</p>
<p>  Type of Wheat	   Tonne   Price/Bushel(FOB)</p>
<p>  Soft White		2,700   $0.27 (over CBOT's March)</p>
<p>(protein max 10.8%)</p>
<p>  Soft White		  800   $0.24 (over CBOT's March)</p>
<p>(protein max 9.5%)</p>
<p>  Hard Red Winter	 3,000   $0.98 (over KCBT's March)</p>
<p>  Dark Northern Spring  3,500   $1.08 (over MGE's March)</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
